1. literal parens, not a macro call: show_arg(value = f(a,b))
2. literal angles, not a macro call: show_arg(value = f<a,b>)
3. nested literal groups: show_arg(value = f(a,g(b,c),d))
4. text around a literal group: show_arg(value = pre(1,2)post)
5. nested commas do not split the outer arg list: show2_args(arg0=f(x,y),arg1=g<p,q>)
6. a real macro call deferred inside an arg still expands: show2_args(arg0=repeat(text=ab,count=2),arg1=plain)
7. a real macro call inside a param expands eagerly: show_param<myparam=repeat(text=ab,count=2)>
8. literal parens inside a param value are preserved: show_param<myparam=f(x,y)>
9. context value used inside a nested deferred call, in its own param list: wrap_deferred
10. same, with the outer param overridden: wrap_deferred<5>
